\pard\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 1r\endash 55v {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Antiphonale officii, Proprium de tempore}}\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24  Beginn mit erstem Advent bis zu den Laudes des Karsamstags. Der Inhalt entspricht Guerrini, Ordinarium, Nr. 14\endash 157. Stark gek\u252 \'fcrzt: bringt von den Offizien meist nur die Ges\u228 \'e4nge zur Vesper des Vorabends, das Invitatorium, die Ges\u228 \'e4nge zu den Benediktionen und zum Magnifikat. Bei hohen Festen auch die Nokturnen (In natali domini, Beschneidung, Epiphanie, Gr\u252 \'fcndonnerstag, Karfreitag, Karsamstag), nach Epiphanie fehlen die Ferialtage. (1r) [Dominica prima in adventu domini]<; (2v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (4v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIIa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (7r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica quarta\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (9v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 In festo sancti Thome\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 < Guerrini Nr. 311; >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 In vigilia natalis domini\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (10v) [In natali domini]; (15v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Per octavas natiuitatis\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (16r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica infra octavas\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (16v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 In festo circumcisione\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (20v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 In vigilia epiphanie\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; [In epiphanie]; (25r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica infra octavas epiphanie\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (25v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica Ia post octavas epiphanie\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (26r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIa post octavas epiphanie\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (26v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIIa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (27r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIIIa<\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 ; (27v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica in LXXa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (28r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica in LXa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (28v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica in La\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (29v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Feria IIIIa in capite ieiunii\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (30r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica prima in XLa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (32v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica II\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 in XLa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (35r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica III in XLa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (37r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica IIII in XLa\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (40r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Dominica in passione\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (42r) [Dominica in ramis]; (42v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Feria quinta in cena domini\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (47r) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Feria VI in parasceve\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <; (51v) >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Sabbato sancto pasche\plain \f2\lang1033\fs22 <.}

